<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#AnnotationActivity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#AnnotationActivity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#AnnotationActivity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A provenance activity that produces a NORMA annotation (i.e. a NormativeContent) from one or more LegalSources."@en .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#AnnotationActivity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#AnnotationActivity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Annotation Activity"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#AnnotatorAgent
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#AnnotatorAgent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#AnnotatorAgent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#AnnotatorAgent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A provenance agent responsible for creating, reviewing, or attesting to a NORMA annotation. May represent a person (legal expert, analyst), a software system (LLM extractor, rule engine), or an organization. For finer-grained typing use the corresponding PROV-O subclasses (prov:Person, prov:SoftwareAgent, prov:Organization). Integrity constraint (not OWL-enforced): for a given NormativeContent, `prov:wasAttributedTo` and `prov:wasAssociatedWith` (via its generating AnnotationActivity) should resolve to the same agent; validate with SHACL."@en .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#AnnotatorAgent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#AnnotatorAgent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Annotator Agent"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#BindingForce
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#BindingForce> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#BindingForce> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#BindingForce> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Binding force of a norm."@en .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#BindingForce> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#BindingForce> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Binding Force"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ComplianceCriticality
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ComplianceCriticality> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ComplianceCriticality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ComplianceCriticality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Criticality level associated with non-compliance with a regulative norm."@en .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ComplianceCriticality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ComplianceCriticality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Compliance Criticality"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ConditionOutcome
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ConditionOutcome> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ConditionOutcome> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ConditionOutcome> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A controlled outcome value produced by evaluating a LegalCondition. It is modelled as an extensible SKOS concept class so binary branches, multi-way gateway branches, exception branches, and decision-table outcomes can all be represented consistently."@en .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ConditionOutcome> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ConditionOutcome> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Condition Outcome"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ConstitutiveRule
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ConstitutiveRule> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ConstitutiveRule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#NormativeContent> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ConstitutiveRule> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#RegulativeNorm> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ConstitutiveRule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A normative content item that defines, classifies, or constitutes a legal concept, status, or institutional fact."@en .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ConstitutiveRule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ConstitutiveRule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Constitutive Rule"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ExtractionMethod
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ExtractionMethod> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ExtractionMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ExtractionMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Method used to produce the annotation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ExtractionMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ExtractionMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Extraction Method"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalAction
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalAction> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalAction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A normalized legal action that is prescribed, prohibited, permitted, or recommended by a regulative norm. NORMA pipeline consumers may work with the literal shortcut `norma:actionText` for low-ceremony use and mint LegalAction individuals only when the knowledge graph needs action-level reuse across norms."@en .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalAction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalAction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Legal Action"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalAgent
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalAgent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalAgent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Agent> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalAgent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An entity that bears the legally relevant role of subject of a regulative norm: the party that is obliged, prohibited, permitted, or recommended to perform a legal action. Instances should be further typed using foaf:Person, foaf:Organization, or foaf:Group to express whether the agent is a natural person, a legal entity (e.g. an AI provider, deployer, or operator), or a collective."@en .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalAgent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalAgent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Legal Agent"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalCondition
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalCondition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A legally relevant condition, fact pattern, or decision criterion whose evaluated outcome determines whether normative content becomes applicable or is triggered. Branch-specific activation is represented using the n-ary TriggerEvent pattern via norma:hasTrigger."@en .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Legal Condition"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalObject
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalObject> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalObject> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The entity, resource, person, document, system, content, or data item toward which the regulated action is directed."@en .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalObject> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalObject> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Legal Object"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalSource
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalSource> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalSource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/ontology#LegalResource> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalSource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A legal resource (in the ELI sense: a work-level identity) from which normative content is extracted, cited, or traced."@en .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalSource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalSource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Legal Source"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalSourceExpression
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalSourceExpression> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalSourceExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/ontology#LegalExpression> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalSourceExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A concrete legal expression of a LegalSource: a specific language, consolidation, or published version of the underlying legal resource. Follows the ELI work/expression pattern: a LegalSource is realised by one or more LegalSourceExpressions via `norma:hasSourceExpression` (subproperty of `eli:is_realized_by`)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalSourceExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#LegalSourceExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Legal Source Expression"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#NegativeRecommendation
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#NegativeRecommendation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#NegativeRecommendation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#RegulativeNorm> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#NormStatus
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#NormStatus> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#NormStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#NormStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Lifecycle status of a normative content item."@en .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#NormStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#NormStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Norm Status"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#NormativeContent
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#NormativeContent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#NormativeContent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#NormativeContent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid11 .
_:genid11 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#allValuesFrom> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/ontology#AdministrativeArea> .
_:genid11 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/ontology#jurisdiction> .
_:genid11 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#NormativeContent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An informational entity that expresses machine-readable legal-normative content extracted or formulated from a legal source, either a regulative norm or a constitutive rule. Jurisdiction is represented only with eli:jurisdiction, whose value must be an eli:AdministrativeArea. If no authoritative URI is available yet, use a local provisional resource typed as eli:AdministrativeArea and provide its rdfs:label."@en .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#NormativeContent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#NormativeContent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Normative Content"@en .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#NormativeContent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Do not attach jurisdiction strings directly to NormativeContent. For extracted labels such as \"Spain\" or \"California\", mint a local jurisdiction resource, type it as eli:AdministrativeArea, attach the extracted text as rdfs:label, and later align or replace it with an authoritative URI when available."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#Obligation
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#Obligation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#Obligation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#RegulativeNorm> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#Permission
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#Permission> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#Permission> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#RegulativeNorm> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#Prohibition
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#Prohibition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#Prohibition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#RegulativeNorm> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#Recommendation
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#Recommendation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#Recommendation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#RegulativeNorm> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#RegulativeNorm
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#RegulativeNorm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#RegulativeNorm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#NormativeContent> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#RegulativeNorm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A normative content item that regulates conduct by prescribing, prohibiting, permitting, or recommending a legal action."@en .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#RegulativeNorm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#RegulativeNorm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Regulative Norm"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ReviewStatus
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ReviewStatus> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ReviewStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ReviewStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Legal review status of an annotation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ReviewStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ReviewStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Review Status"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#TriggerEvent
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#TriggerEvent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#TriggerEvent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid12 .
_:genid12 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onClass> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#NormativeContent> .
_:genid12 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#qualifiedCardinality> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger> .
_:genid12 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#activatesNorm> .
_:genid12 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#TriggerEvent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid13 .
_:genid13 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onClass> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#ConditionOutcome> .
_:genid13 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#qualifiedCardinality> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger> .
_:genid13 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#hasOutcome> .
_:genid13 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#TriggerEvent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Reified instance of the triggering relation between a legal condition, one evaluated condition outcome, and one activated normative content item. Represents true, false, and other branch-specific activations without using separate branch-label datatype properties. Follows Pattern 1 / Use Case 1 of the W3C Working Group Note Defining N-ary Relations on the Semantic Web."@en .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#TriggerEvent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/norma-ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/norma-ontology#TriggerEvent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Trigger Event"@en .
